# zdev projects — one path per line, relative to $ZDEV_WORKSPACE (default
# ~/workspace). Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored.
#
# TWO MODES:
#
# Classic (default): this file is the whole registry — every project is a
# line here.
#
# Discovery (ZDEV_PROJECTS_DISCOVER=1 in ~/.config/zdev/env): the workspace
# layout is the registry and this file holds OVERRIDES only —
#
#   Group-ness is an EXPLICIT on-disk marker, never inferred from
#   directory shape, and never answered in config:
#   - root dir WITH .git          → a plain project row (zdev, dotfiles)
#   - root dir + INITIATIVE.md    → an INITIATIVE: its own dir rows as the
#                                    group home, plus one row per child that
#                                    has .git (so notes/ never rows)
#   - root dir + .zdev            → a DRAWER: one row per child dir, any dir
#                                    (e.g. projects/). .zdev is an empty
#                                    marker file (TOML format reserved for
#                                    future group metadata — display name,
#                                    colour, per-group collapse — none of
#                                    which exists yet; only its EXISTENCE is
#                                    checked today, never its contents)
#   - root dir with NEITHER       → INVISIBLE — no rows at all. A stray
#                                    non-git dir with no marker (archive/,
#                                    a Downloads-ish folder) never pollutes
#                                    the fleet. `zdev doctor` flags any
#                                    directory that would have rowed under
#                                    the old implicit rule.
#   `touch <group>/.zdev` makes a drawer; `touch <group>/INITIATIVE.md`
#   makes an initiative (deleting either demotes/hides it again).
#
# The daemon watches the workspace: `git clone` into a marked group IS
# add-repo, `rm -rf` is remove — rows follow the disk in seconds.
# `zdev --list-projects -v` shows why every row exists.
#
# Either mode: append ' *' to mark a favorite — started by `zdev up`,
# never reaped:
#   projects/backend *
#
# Replace the examples below with your own (delete them entirely under
# discovery unless you want favorites or off-convention paths).
dotfiles
projects/api
projects/web *
